cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AILIT_TRAVEL: Replication Archive"
message: >-
  This archive accompanies a manuscript currently under anonymous peer review.
  Citation metadata will be populated upon acceptance.
type: software
version: "1.0.0-preprint"
date-released: "2026-05-30"
authors:
  - name: "Author information withheld during anonymous peer review"
abstract: >-
  Replication archive for a sentence-embedding-based cross-national analysis of
  national AI-in-education policy text adoption against three independent AI
  competency frameworks (UNESCO Student, UNESCO Teacher, and OECD-European
  Commission AI Literacy Framework). Contains anchor sentences, adherence
  matrices, robustness battery outputs, clustering results, and figures for the
  25-country corpus.
keywords:
  - AI literacy
  - AI competency frameworks
  - cross-national policy analysis
  - sentence-embedding alignment
  - hierarchical clustering
license: "MIT"
